sequenceDiagram
  title: Platform Adapter — Lua module → interface → platform impl (ThreadKind)

  participant LUA as Lua code
  participant MOD as modules.init_* — dialog/notify/clipboard/openurl/store
  participant INTF as C++ interface — coconut.dialog / packages.*
  participant PLAT as platform impl — darwin/win/linux
  participant OS as NSAlert / MessageBoxW / GTK
  participant BGC as background stubs

  LUA ->> MOD : init_all(lua, kind)

  alt kind == Main
    MOD ->> MOD : register real closure on coconut.* table
  else kind == Background
    MOD ->> BGC : register warning stub — main-only APIs
    BGC -->> LUA : returns false — "[bg] … requires the main thread"
  end

  LUA ->> MOD : coconut.dialog.message("Saved!", "App", "info")
  MOD ->> INTF : dialog::messageBox(title, message, kind)
  INTF ->> PLAT : per-OS dispatch — NSAlert / MessageBoxW / GTK
  PLAT ->> OS : native modal dialog
  OS -->> PLAT : button pressed — OK/Cancel
  PLAT -->> INTF : dialog::Result { confirmed }
  INTF -->> MOD : sol::table { confirmed, path, paths }
  MOD -->> LUA : result table

  @start_note right of PLAT
    Platform events call back into bridge events:
    lifecycle::registerEvents (resize/focus/blur) →
    ctx:emit → __coconut_dispatch_event → coconut.on().
  @end_note